sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch05-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch05-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.51" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.508"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Compensation versus independent reduction can be compared in birds with reduced wings and in a few genetic models of trait loss. Superfluous is not an independent measurement in those tables, which lowers the force of a positive result. The anti-necessity wording is easier to support, with single well-measured counterexamples to obligatory trade-offs, than the claim that selection always removes every superfluous part." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: On phylogenies, score reduction of structures that have lost their function and ask whether a neighbouring structure enlarges in compensation. Reduction without obligatory enlargement would support the economy clause; enlargement that always requires reduction of an adjoining part would refute that clause. The always-reduced clause would be refuted by functionless structures that are retained without a detectable cost." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Superfluous is often inferred from the reduction, which circularly supports the claim.", "Allometry creates apparent trade-offs that are not nutritional compensation.", "Gene loss and morphological compensation are rarely measured in the same species." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch05-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch05-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.56" ;
